> He stings you again; TTL 7.
> Round ends; TTL 6.
> Timeouts; TTL 5.

Um, why did TTL go down twice in succession there?

> He stings; TTL 2.
> You move.
> He stings; TTL 1.
> You move.
> Timeouts; You die.
> 
> It seems to me that it doesn't actually matter where the player was in
> their move sequence for this one; they always get three moves.

Here's my guess at how it would work if you start on a single move and
use it to move next to Demogorgon (or perhaps to heal yourself in an
ongoing combat with him):

You move next to Demogorgon:
He stings: TTL 20.
He stings again: TTL 7.
Turn ends, movement points doled out.
Timeouts: TTL 6.

You move.
He stings: TTL 3.
You move.
He stings: TTL 2.
Turn ends, movement points doled out.
Timeouts: TTL 1.

So that's two chances you had to swing at him before you needed to
heal.  In other words, I _think_, not only is it safe to get into a
whack-heal cycle with Demogorgon, it is also safe to get into a
whack-whack-heal cycle with him.
